Responsibilities

• Develop and implement a cohesive technology strategy that aligns with the company's business goals, focusing on accelerating growth and enhancing competitive advantage. Ensure our trading infrastructure supports high-volume, low-latency trading with maximum uptime;

• Lead the technology team by fostering an innovative, collaborative, and high-performance culture. Mentor and develop the team to ensure they are proficient in the latest technologies and methodologies;

• Drive technological innovation to improve trading platforms, back-office systems, and client-facing applications. Ensure our technology stack is scalable, reliable, and can support rapid growth and international expansion;

• Oversee the development and implementation of robust cybersecurity measures to protect client data and company assets. Ensure compliance with international financial regulations and standards;

• Negotiate and manage relationships with software vendors, technology partners, and service providers to ensure they meet the company's standards for quality and service;

• Regularly review and optimize the performance of the IT infrastructure and systems to ensure they meet the demands of the business, including high transaction volumes and fast execution speeds;

• Ensure that technology initiatives drive improved user experience and customer satisfaction. Be proactive in identifying and implementing technology solutions that meet the evolving needs of traders;

• Stay abreast of new trends and technologies in the financial and tech industries. Evaluate and propose the adoption of new technologies that can benefit the company.

Requirements

• At least 10 years of experience in a technology role

• At least 5 years on leadership position as CTO, Director of Engineering etc

• Proven track record of developing and executing technology strategies that have contributed to measurable business growth;

• Engineering background with extensive experience in software development, IT infrastructure, data engineering, cybersecurity, and IT operations;

• Strong leadership and team development skills, with the ability to inspire and motivate a high-performing technology team;

• Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with stakeholders at all levels;

• Comprehension of core compliance standards, governance, and regulatory requirements.

• A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.

• Fluent in East Slavic languages;

Will be a plus

• Experience in financial services or trading industry, ideally with a strong background in developing and optimising trading platforms like MT4 and MT5;

• AI fluency and awareness of current AI methodologies and best practices within tech operations;

• An MBA or equivalent experience in business management is highly desirable;

• Willingness to work from Cyprus office.

We offer

• Holding a C-level position with the authority to shape and implement the company’s technological strategy by fostering innovation and product improvement, while also supporting stable business growth;

• The opportunity to collaborate with a large, strong engineering organization of 180+ professionals

• Gaining invaluable experience working on a global scale, collaborating with diverse cultures, expanding new markets and your professional horizons;

• Being a part of a company committed to revolutionising the trading industry, known for its customer-centric approach and innovative solutions;

• Annual health budget after the probation period;

• Public holidays according to the list set by the company;

• 10 paid sick leave days per year;

• Flight tickets, hotel or apartment accommodation, migration support for you and your family (if relocating);

• Opportunity for growth and professional development.

